<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>On the real opinion page, clicking a cited case or pressing Enter / ↓ opens a pinned bottom panel. Previous / next moves through its actual occurrences in the opinion and reports <em>Occurrence N of M</em>, wrapping at either end. A hover preview stays compact and does not replace a pinned selection. Escape or Close returns to the current citation; Open case follows the cited opinion link.</p>
  <p>Treatment details and Full analysis appear when an Authorities record supplies them. A plain opinion link without that record explicitly reports unavailable analysis; it does not infer a treatment. Try the two Saucier links in <a href="/opinion/145918/">Pearson v. Callahan</a>, or use the complete <a href="/pages/opinion-page/">opinion-page example</a>.</p>
  <p>The same reader opens footnotes in a popover, offers copy actions for selected text, and searches within the opinion with <kbd>/</kbd>.</p>
</div>

